# IEC 61850 GOOSE subscriber (<iec61850-rtu>, ww-n29; bennu's module is never built, so there is no oracle and the DUT is ours).
# go-iec61850 (MIT, independent of iec61850-rs) publishes PUB's gcbTrip from substation.scd on lo; device.xml subscribes twice: from
# the same SCD by RTU1's ExtRef (intAddr mirror), and from sub.cid's SEL block as bennu does (a TRIP writes false to trip). The writes
# reach provider.py, the stand-in provider in the peers container. GOOSE needs CAP_NET_RAW in the DUT container and lo as the segment.
CFG=${CFG:-${here:-/conformance}/${proto:-iec61850-rtu}/device.xml}
DUT_DEFAULT=rust
DUT_CAPS='--cap-add NET_RAW'
DUT_EXTRA="conformance/iec61850-rtu/substation.scd:/tmp/substation.scd conformance/iec61850-rtu/sub.cid:/tmp/sub.cid"
STOCK_CMD='echo "bennu never builds its IEC 61850 module: run with DUT=rust" >&2; exit 2'
WARMUP=3
CAPTURE_FILTER='ether proto 0x88b8 or tcp port 5555'
PROTO_FILTER=goose
ZEEK_LOAD=''
